  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, thanks for reaching out. I checked and you're right: Duo was never set up on your account, and that's why the VPN keeps asking for it. The good news is that your account and your new laptop both look fine. Setting up Duo takes a short session (about 10–15 minutes) with a technician, either remote or in person, and you'll need your phone with you. To get ready: 1) If you can, install the Duo Mobile app on your phone from the App Store or Google Play. 2) Reply with a few times that work for you, and say whether you'd like a remote or in-person session. In the session, the technician will make sure Duo is installed on your laptop, have you scan a setup code with your phone, and send a test request to confirm it works. Until then, the VPN probably won't connect. If you need anything urgently before then, let us know.",
